class_name KinbookLines
extends RefCounted
## What's on Kinbook, the town's social media (Kinbook, on the phone).
## Three corners of it: Charlatown Rants & Raves (anonymous complaints and
## thank-yous), Are We Dating the Same Fella? (anonymous call-outs), and
## ChipIn fundraisers (the town's GoFundMe, mostly for things people did to
## themselves).
##
## Kinbook is the trashy corner of the game, on purpose: the comments are
## the joke. Threads wander off topic into fights about politics, who dated
## who, and outing whoever posted "anonymously". On an island everyone has
## dated the same five people, and the comments all admit it. That stays
## implied, never explicit. The joke's still never on someone who's
## actually struggling. Made-up people only, first names and an initial,
## the way these groups look.
##
## A comment is [who, text], or [who, text, true] for a reply under the one
## before. "closed": true ends a thread with the admin turning comments off.

